  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Pontryagin invariants and integral formulas for Milnor's triple linking number — To each three-component link in the 3-sphere, we associate a geometrically natural characteristic map from the 3-torus\n\n**Pontryagin invariants and integral formulas for Milnor's triple linking number**\n\n*DENNIS DETURCK, HERMAN GLUCK, RAFAL KOMENDARCZYK*\n\n60 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** To each three-component link in the 3-sphere, we associate a geometrically natural characteristic map from the 3-torus to the 2-sphere, and show that the pairwise linking numbers and Milnor triple linking number that classify the link up to link ho- motopy correspond to the Pontryagin invariants that classify its characteristic map up to homotopy. This can be viewed as a natural extension of the familiar fact that the linking number of a two-component link in 3-space is the degree of its associated Gauss map from the 2-torus to the 2-sphere. When the pairwise linking numbers are all zero, we give an integral formula for the triple linking number analogous to the Gauss integral for the pairwise linking numbers.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 The Milnor -invariant; 3 The Pontryagin -invariant; 4 Explicit formulas for the characteristic map; 5 The Pontryagin -invariant of the characteris; 6 Proof of Theorem ??; 7 Sketch of an algebraic proof of Theorem ??; 8 Proof of Theorem ??, formulas (1) and (2); 9 Fourier series and the Proof of Theorem ??, ; Appendix. Whitehead's integral formula for the; References",
